- op: discuss  # abe2
  at: '2026-09-06T13:48:25Z'  # abe2
  by: agent  # abe2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # abe2
  clock: 3  # abe2
  nonce: abe2  # abe2
  message: "SCOPED 2026-09-06, read-only, before the fix (next on the arc after WI-dupok). Shape (b) -- disclose only the grants that were LOAD-BEARING for this verdict -- and where each piece already lives:\n\nTHE SET. verify_claims._uncatalogued_external_modules (~2790-3005) walks every external call edge the classifier did not match, expands the module slot into its disjuncts (INV-zimud), and at\n    if disjuncts and not unenumerated: continue\na module has just been declared an EXAMINED NEGATIVE by a module_completeness grant -- shipped catalogue or overlay, the gate cannot tell. That `continue` IS the load-bearing set; the function returns only `unknown`. The change is a sibling collection (`vouched: dict[language, set[module]]`, the spellings that matched, keyed by which catalogue matched -- `catalog.module_io_is_enumerated(s)` already runs per language) returned beside `unknown` (or a small result dataclass), carried on BoundaryCoverage by compute_boundary_coverage (~3750, the one computation site every verdict path shares -- the same reason method_call_blind_languages and suppressed_sink_methods live there), so no caller can forget it.\n\nTHE DISCLOSURE. catalog_provenance() (~1655-1700) builds `completeness_grants` from the OVERLAY FILES (one record per file that vouches for a module, INV-tabaf) -- it never looks at the run, which is why a shipped grant is disclosed nowhere and why the count is 0/0 on every arm of the WI-nolut and WI-komun A/Bs. Shape (b) adds a run-derived key, `load_bearing_grants: [{language, module, source}]` where source is \"shipped\" (the language's io_primitives yaml) or the overlay path, populated from coverage.vouched; render_catalog_provenance_text prints it as its own block beside the overlay grants (\"this clean verdict rests on N enumerated modules: python errno, struct, ... (shipped catalogue, dated 2026-09-06); telnetlib (overlay deps.yaml)\"). Both arms consume it (boundary and taint verdicts share compute_boundary_coverage), so INV-nuhun's asymmetry does not recur.\n\nWHY (b) AND NOT (a), restated with today's numbers: python now carries 121 grants and javascript 10; printing every shipped grant on every run is the always-there disclosure a reader discounts (LIVE rule: a caveat that is always there is discounted). The load-bearing set is small by construction -- the modules THIS repository called into unclassified -- and it answers the reader's actual question: which dated audits does my clean verdict stand on?\n\nTESTS to mirror: test_vouched_modules_disclosure.py (JSON envelope key, text block, origin kept apart, empty when nothing vouched). Add: a repo calling struct.pack (granted 2026-09-06) yields load_bearing_grants [{python, struct, shipped}] and coverage.complete True; a repo calling only classified calls yields []; an overlay-granted module reports the overlay path as source; a language with no grants used yields nothing.\n\nDOCS: VERIFY-CLAIMS-SCOPE.md §\"A module_completeness grant in your overlay turns a gate OFF\" gains the sentence WI-lavut says is missing -- the shipped catalogues make the same claim, and the run names the ones a clean verdict rested on.\n\nMEASURE: the js cohort (jsleg_completeness_09062026, out/new) and the python cohort (dupok_python_09062026) already have cold verdicts; re-run one repo per cohort and read the new block. No verdict CATEGORY should move -- this is disclosure only -- and that non-movement is the check."  # abe2
