- op: discuss  # 2ec3
  at: '2026-09-06T15:01:48Z'  # 2ec3
  by: agent  # 2ec3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2ec3
  clock: 5  # 2ec3
  nonce: 2ec3  # 2ec3
  message: "DONE 2026-09-06 (PR #806), shape (b) as scoped above. The load-bearing set is the gate's own `continue` (a call into a module no row classified and a grant declared examined), collected in one walk shared with the unknown set (_adjudicate_external_modules, so the two cannot disagree), carried as BoundaryCoverage.load_bearing_grants (language -> sorted modules) from compute_boundary_coverage, passed into catalog_provenance(load_bearing=...) as the block's only run-derived key, rendered in text mode whether or not anything was user-supplied (\"NOTE: the coverage gate PASSED these modules on completeness grants ... Every confirmed verdict above rests on them\"). Shipped and overlay grants are listed alike; an overlay's file-derived completeness_grants stay beside it. Tests: test_load_bearing_grants.py (the set, both surfaces, the old-shape guard, the no-move controls). Docs: VERIFY-CLAIMS-SCOPE.md.\n\nMEASURED, disclosure only (measured at the branch tip on four cohort repos with cold caches -- express, pm2, winston from the javascript cohort and httpx from the python cohort: 16 of 16 per-claim verdicts identical to each cohort's own prior arm; the block lists 25 python grants on httpx, 5 javascript + 4 python on pm2, 4 javascript on winston, and none on express, whose granted-module calls are all rowed and whose node:-spelled import edges are a separate emission defect, filed; instrument and read-back in lavut_grants_09062026/).\n\nRESIDUAL: the grants are named by module, not by their `retrieved` date; a reader wanting the date goes to the catalogue's module_completeness block, which the text block points at. Adding the date per module is a one-line extension once anyone asks for it."  # 2ec3
